WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.060
A new month brings a new batch of content
to stream on Netflix.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.260
From a Netflix Original movie that will make
you swoon to new series to binge, here are

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.709
the best movies and TV shows to watch on Netflix
in February 2021.

00:00:14.199 --> 00:00:19.440
Perhaps the biggest Netflix Original movie
of February 2021 is the long-awaited third

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.250
and final installment in the To All the Boys
cinematic franchise: To All the Boys: Always

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.250
and Forever.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.000
Based on author Jenny Han's novel Always and
Forever, Lara Jean, the film picks up after

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.890
the events of To All the Boys: P.S.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:38.160
I Still Love You, which saw Lara Jean Covey
enduring a rough patch with her fake-boyfriend-turned-real-boyfriend

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.160
Peter Kavinsky.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.170
In To All the Boys: Always and Forever, Lara
Jean embarks on two trips that will completely

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.120
change her life and cause her to reevaluate
what her future will look like after she graduates

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.120
high school.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.070
Will Peter and Lara Jean stick together in
the end, or will Lara Jean decide she wants

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:58.340
to spread her wings and be a single, independent
butterfly as she heads off to college?

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.850
You'll have to wait until the movie hits Netflix
on February 12 to find out.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.670
Before then, though, there are a number of
fantastic Netflix Original flicks to get excited

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.670
about.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:12.229
On February 3, Black Beach, about a lawyer
facing his dark past after he reunites with

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.740
an old friend, and All My Friends Are Dead,
about a group of friends' memorable New Year's

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.719
Eve party, drop on Netflix.

00:01:18.719 --> 00:01:23.189
February 5 brings the black-and-white drama
Malcolm &amp; Marie, which centers on the title

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:27.509
characters unraveling the darker parts of
their relationship during the night of Malcolm's

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:28.509
movie premiere.

00:01:29.509 --> 00:01:34.270
Though Netflix is getting into the lovey-dovey
spirit in February 2021, that doesn't mean

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:37.710
that all its film offerings for the month
skew toward the romantic.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:42.409
Some do, but others hit all sorts of other
emotions, sure to satisfy the various types

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:44.509
of cinephiles out there all month long.

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:53.630
"You mustn't be afraid to dream a little bigger,
darling."

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.609
Looking to revisit a mind-bending Christopher
Nolan film?

00:01:56.609 --> 00:01:59.749
Stream Inception on Netflix beginning on February
1.

00:01:59.749 --> 00:02:04.820
Want to distract yourself from the candy-hearts-and-cutesy-card-filled
holiday of February and remember the cheery

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.550
days of December, all while laughing at Chevy
Chase's wild antics?

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:12.950
National Lampoon's Christmas Vacation is the
movie for you, and it's arriving on Netflix

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.610
on the first of the month.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:19.020
Action movie fans will want to set aside some
time to watch Jason Statham in The Bank Job,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:25.200
about the Baker Street robbery that took place
in London in 1971, on February 1, and War

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.430
Dogs, starring Miles Teller and Jonah Hill
as two arms dealers carrying out a massive

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.010
ammo supply deal, on February 8.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.570
The first of the month brings Martin Scorsese's
jaw-dropping psychological thriller Shutter

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:41.970
Island, while later, on February 21, both
The Conjuring and The Conjuring 2 arrive to

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.490
the streamer's digital shelves.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.960
Near the end of the month, on February 26,
queue up two movies that are returning to

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:53.060
Netflix after some time away, and one that's
new to the platform: Captain Fantastic, a

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.680
comedy-drama about a family emerging from
a decade-long isolation and rejoining society;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:02.070
No Escape, the action-thriller starring Owen
Wilson as a family man stuck in a foreign

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:07.580
country amid an uprising; and Our Idiot Brother,
featuring Paul Rudd as the titular character

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.270
who gives his three sisters all sorts of grief.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:16.210
Netflix Original series to keep your eyes
on throughout February 2021 include Firefly

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:20.980
Lane, a drama following two best friends who
experience trials and tribulations throughout

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:26.170
their 30 years of companionship; The Crew,
a comedy set in a NASCAR garage where a seasoned

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:30.930
crew chief clashes with his team of millennial
staff; and Ginny &amp; Georgia, which follows

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:34.810
the title characters as their small family
settles down in New England.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.950
Additionally, you'll want to make some space
in your Netflix queue for Nadiya Bakes, a

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.430
cookery series featuring Nadiya Hussain of
The Great British Bake-Off fame, which will

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.300
hit the streamer on February 12.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:50.200
Early on in the month, the platform is scooping
up the third installment of the anthology

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.640
series The Sinner, this one centered on a
man named Jamie Burns; viewers can stream

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.360
it beginning on February 6.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.510
If more family-friendly fare is what you're
after this February, the first two seasons

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:04.780
of Nickelodeon's iCarly, arriving on the 8th
of the month, should do the trick.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.030
Looking to balance laughs with thrills next
month?

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:12.101
Check out the third season of NBC's Good Girls,
starring Christina Hendricks, Retta, and Mae

00:04:12.101 --> 00:04:16.389
Whitman as three mothers who decide to take
their fates and their finances in their own

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.660
hands by robbing a supermarket.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.439
Good Girls season 3 will be available to stream
starting on February 16.

00:04:23.439 --> 00:04:28.620
Speaking of heart-racing, February 24 marks
the arrival of the second season of Two Sentence

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.990
Horror Stories, the anthology series comprised
of 30-minute horror shorts.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:37.310
The episodes will air on the CW throughout
January before hitting Netflix at the end

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.310
of February.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:44.150
Both the stand-up comedy and documentary sections
of Netflix's library will grow a bit bigger

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.840
in February, starting with the arrival of
season 2 of the Emmy-winning special Tiffany

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:53.379
Haddish Presents: They Ready and the Netflix
debut of Strip Down, Rise Up.

00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:57.569
In this collection of They Ready, Haddish
introduces six of her favorite comedians who

00:04:57.569 --> 00:05:00.139
will perform short but hilarious sets.

00:05:00.139 --> 00:05:04.710
Strip Down, Rise Up is a documentary that
explores how women who pole dance are reclaiming

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:08.710
their authority, autonomy, and confidence
through "movement and meaning."

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:13.710
A few days later, on February 10, the true
crime documentary Crime Scene: The Vanishing

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.469
at the Cecil Hotel arrives on Netflix.

00:05:16.469 --> 00:05:21.800
The first in a series of documentaries focused
on crime-scene locations, The Vanishing at

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.449
Cecil Hotel recounts the events that took
place leading up to, during, and after the

00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:31.740
disappearance and death of Elisa Lam, a Canadian
student whose body was found in the Cecil

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.949
Hotel's water tank.

00:05:32.949 --> 00:05:37.599
For a markedly more lighthearted documentary
experience, check out Pelé, which tells the

00:05:37.599 --> 00:05:42.729
story of how the ultra-famous Brazilian footballer
became the sports icon he's remembered as

00:05:42.729 --> 00:05:43.729
today.

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:46.069
Pelé hits Netflix on February 23.

00:05:46.069 --> 00:05:50.169
That same day, Brian Regan's stand-up special
On the Rocks will be available to stream on

00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:55.819
Netflix, and on the 12th the month, Hate by
Dani Rovira also joins the Netflix library.

00:05:56.819 --> 00:06:01.080
Early in the month, Erased and Lila &amp; Eve
will depart from Netflix — followed by Don't

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.680
Knock Twice on February 7 and A Bad Moms Christmas
on February 10.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.419
The following day, the Will Ferrell-Mark Wahlberg
buddy cop movie The Other Guys will have its

00:06:10.419 --> 00:06:13.029
final day in the sun on the streaming platform.

00:06:13.029 --> 00:06:17.710
On Valentine's Day, both Alone in Berlin and
Hostiles say goodbye to Netflix.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:22.569
Other notable films leaving Netflix in February
include the hilarious and charming Emma Stone

00:06:22.569 --> 00:06:27.749
comedy Easy A, the classic Scorsese crime
film Goodfellas, the heart-wrenching romantic

00:06:27.749 --> 00:06:33.530
drama A Walk to Remember, and Clint Eastwood's
2008 drama Gran Torino.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.479
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:39.919
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
Netflix originals are coming soon.

00:06:39.919 --> 00:06:44.029
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

